{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547951-re-inventing-the-wheel-hunter-endowment-hack","id":1547951,"title":"Re-inventing the Wheel [Hunter Endowment Hack]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-25T16:22:17-08:00","id":1547951,"title":"Re-inventing the Wheel [Hunter Endowment Hack]","content":"So for a while, I have worked on certain capacity on developing my Personal &quot;Hunterverse&quot;, which divided Hunter orgs according to a certain &quot;type&quot; as well as rebuilding Endowments into something more flexible. The reason for the later is twofold- first, I really <i>hate</i> writing powers. Even as a player finding which spell I find interesting is a tenacious process which I just don't enjoy, and in general I prefer more open systems. Second, it gives that weird &quot;anime&quot; feeling, where the characters have access to some specific form of power which they find new ways to improvise and control it. So having something which is limited on one hand and flexible on the other is something that I found of interest, and while working on the different &quot;gods&quot; for my Fantasy Shard (where they are basically Endowment sources), I decided to go back to my Endowment project and start building the different orgs around them.<br /> <br /> So, how do &quot;Flexible Endowments work?<br /> <br /> First, each Endowment is executed by using Applications- which work similarly to the open Blood Magic system from Vampire. Each Application is rated 1-5, and it defines what the Endowment attempts to achieve. For most rolls (unless the ST decides otherwise), the player needs 1 Success per Application used- as hunters, who don't really &quot;get&quot; the supernatural, have harder and harder time to grasp how to combine different aspects of their power. In general, Applications of Endowments lean heavily towards fighting the darkness, though there are numerous methods through which it can be achieved. Here is the current list of Applications used in the system-<br /> <br /> <u>Applications</u><br /> Abjuration- disrupts supernatural powers (suppress a Bygone's power, break a spell's hold, etc)<br /> <br /> Affliction- inflicts negative conditions upon the target (enforce a negative Condition, Tilt or penalty)<br /> <br /> Booning- gives positive influence to yourself or other (gives a positive Condition or modifier)<br /> <br /> Divination- find information related to the target (gathers Clues, gives prophetic dream, see the unseen, etc)<br /> <br /> Exorcism- banish or harm spiritual entities (end Manifestation Conditions, enchant an object into a Bane, enforce a Ban, etc)<br /> <br /> Rejuvenation- purifies the body or the soul (heals damage, removes Conditions and Tilts of mundane origin)<br /> <br /> Summoning- invokes or commune with spiritual beings or worlds (speak with a ghost, summon a spirit, control an angel)<br /> <br /> Vanquishment- causes direct damage (throw fire ball, enchant a blade, turn water into acid)<br /> <br /> Warding- Protects against the supernatural (create a spiritual barrier, turn a place into a holy ground, turn a person invisible to the supernatural)<br /> <br /> Each Endowment have 3 favoured Application, which are bought by the price of Endowment while others cost 5 Experience per dot, as well as 3 Themes which define it- an Endowment should, ideally, act while resonating with all three Themes, and the less Themes it answers the more difficult it is to use it. Additionally, each Endowment has a set of Attributes related to it- either following the Physical/Mental/Social categories, or by following the Power/Finesse/Resistance categories. The ST choose one Attribute from that category for the roll according to the specific Application in mind.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Endowments work better some enemies over others- as such, each Endowment has 3 Favoured Enemies, as well as one specialty within those Enemies. Not all monsters belong to a certain Enemy category, and the ST is to decide to which category a monster belongs if any. The following is the list of Enemies available, as well as example Specialities-<br /> <br /> <u>Enemies</u><br /> Vampirism (Kindred, Ghouls, Strix)<br /> <br /> Shamanism (Shapeshifters, Claimed, Spirits)<br /> <br /> Witchcraft (Mages, Hallows, Supernal Entities)<br /> <br /> Alchemy (Prometheans, Alchemists, Qashmallim)<br /> <br /> Hedge Magic (Changelings,Fetches, Hobgoblins)<br /> <br /> Necromancy (Bound, Ghosts, Reapers)<br /> <br /> Sorcery (Mummies, Sorcerers, Fiends)<br /> <br /> Theurgy (Angels, Demons, Infrastructures)<br /> <br /> Dreamwalking (Beasts, Heroes, Goetia)<br /> <br /> Deviance (Deviants, Manticores)<br /> <br /> Slashing (Slashers, Hunters, Mysterious Places)<br /> <br /> Infernalism (Dominions, Larvae, Immundi)<br /> <br /> Eldritch Magic (Acamoth, Gulmoth, Intruders)<br /> <br /> Contagion (Infected, Carriers, Hunger)<br /> <br /> Finally, there is the Cost- each Endowment roll has a Cost associated with it, generally either Lethal Damage or Willpower, but some use a more exotic approach. The roll takes 1 unit of Cost per Application used, unless the ST deems otherwise. And with that in mind, the roll for a Flexible Endowment should look something like this-<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Application + Favoured Attribute + Endowment Equation Value [can be beyond +/-5]<br /> <br /> <b>Modifiers</b>: Used not in Theme [-1 for each Theme violated], +1 for a favoured Enemy, +1 for specialised target, -1 for Enemy not in the favoured list (but which can be described by it)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: see each Endowment section<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Failure:</b> using the supernatural is always playing with fire, and sometimes it turns against the hunter. The hunter suffers not only from a Backlash, but a complication arises of the same magnitude and in favour of a monstrous entity to the ST\u2019s choosing.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>a Backlash, as described in the Endowment entry, appears<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> the hunter channels their will to control the eldritch power. The Endowment manifested as requested.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> the hunter finds the use of the Endowment as easy as breathing. They do not need to spend the required cost.<br /> <br /> While that describes the roll for the Endowments- it does not describe the orgs themselves. Each organization is being defined through a short writeup- most already have well defined writeups in either canon books or in fan wirteups. Some orgs in the project, however, are going to be all new- if there will be interest I will provide more information about those orgs, but currently, each org is described in the following scheme-<br /> <br /> <u>Organization Template</u><br /> <b>Concept</b>: what the organization is about- why do they hunt and the basis of their ideology<br /> <br /> <b>Sphere</b>: the organization\u2019s sphere of influence, geographically speaking<br /> <br /> <b>Endowments</b>: the supernatural power that the organization provide<br /> <br /> <b>Key</b>: the source behind the organization\u2019s Endowments<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>: what does it take to gain access to the organization and its Endowments<br /> <br /> <b>Foundation</b>: a basic ability bestowed through the act of initiation<br /> <br /> <b>Backlash</b>: the consequence for failing the Endowment roll<br /> <br /> <b>Themes</b>: three themes which define what the Endowment can do<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: what resource is spent while activating the Endowment<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: three Applications through which the Endowment more naturally manifests itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: the Attribute category which is used to produce the effects of the Endowment, either Mental/Social/Physical or Power/Finesse/Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: three enemies favoured by the Endowment, with one of the subcategories having a speciality in parenthesis<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bAnd that's it! Currently Compacts are done, so I am going to post them shortly after this post. Hope you will find this of interest!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-25T16:41:52-08:00","id":1547952,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Compacts</b></u><br /> Compacts refer to a certain type of Hunter organizations- specifically, to organizations which are relatively small in scale and very cohesive, or wide in scale and very diffused. Because Compacts lack the same resources and authority that other orgs has, the larger the Compact, the harder it is to control its members, and the harder it is to guarantee their devotion through support and resources. Still, in this setting, each Compact has their own Endowment which they use to hunt, and their all united around the concept of the Vigil as in hunting down the darkness for a variety of reasons. If you don't see a compact you know in here, it is not because they don't exist in the setting, but because they have a better organizational category to define them- after all, Compacts, in this setting, are defined by their independence and devotion to the Vigil. Organizations which are integrated in some manner to a wider structure (such as a religion or a state), or which have less aggressive attitude towards the supernatural (such as seeking to study it or support other hunters rather than doing the work themselves), have their own categories instead.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ashwood Abbey (Core)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: hellfire club of hedonistic hunters who celebrate their darkest desires through hunting down monsters<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: British Isles<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Bacchanal Projections<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: The Black Licence<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: after going through the Initiation Ceremony where the candidate must survive their hunt against a monster, if they manage to take down their enemy they are offered to add their name to the local member book, sanctioned by the License<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: by accepting their own dark desires, the hunter\u2019s carnal nature becomes overwhelming. They gain another Vice, though they can only fulfill one per session for Willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: sinking deep into vice, the hunter becomes disillusioned by their own ideals. They can not gain Willpower from fulfilling their Virtue until they fulfill their Vice first, even if they can not gain Willpower from the act.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Carnal</b>- Bacchanal Projections utilise the darkest desires of the target, instigating them and drawing power from them<br /> <br /> <b>Transgressed</b>- Bacchanal Projections drive the targets to break taboos, be them social or spiritual, and draw power from those acts<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle</b>- Bacchanal Projections are not obvious distortion of reality, rather working by mental manipulations and sensory distortions<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Affliction, Booning<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Social<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Slashing [Slashers], Infernalism, Dreamwalking<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dies Irae (S&amp;B)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: demon hunters who used heretical magic to transform themselves into infernal beings<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Art of Dying<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: the Ars Moriendi book<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: by invoking the First Transformation of the Ars Moriendi, the user have their physical and spiritual forms reconstructed to allow applications of the occult power<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the First Transformation, which mutilates the flesh of the user, allowing them to interact with beings in the Twilight.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the demonic power takes over the hunter. They must act to fulfill their Vice in the most brutal and quick manner possible. They do not gain Willpower from the act, though it doesn\u2019t count against the limit on fulfilling one\u2019s Vice.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Mutilating</b>- the Art of Dying transforms the flesh of the user, always causing them some sort of demonic transformation<br /> <br /> <b>Vengeful</b>- the Art of Dying is powered by pain and anger, targeting those who have harmed the hunter<br /> <br /> <b>Terrifying</b>- the Art of Dying bestows terrible presence upon the user, inflicting fear on lesser demons<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Lethal Damage<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Exorcism, Rejuvenation, Vanquishment<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Power<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Infernalism [Possessed], Sorcery, Eldritch Magic<br /> <br /> <u><b>Heritage House (DE: DS, GotU)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: Blood sworn hunters who are cursed by fate and dream to maintain generational Vigil<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA<br /> <br /> <i>Endowment</i>: Sanguine Bonds<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Accepting the generation curse which haunts the families<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: After being afflicted by their generational curse, they need to survive the curse\u2019s Night of Haunting, which takes the form of a dream quest into their own family\u2019s history. Those who survive gain access to the Endowment.<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: Those who are marked by the generational curse are able to sense the presence of both the enemies of the clan and those born to it with a scene, by rolling Occult + Wits.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the generational curse of the hunter triggers. A vampire of proper magnitude (depends on the Endowment Value) will get haunted to target them in some manner.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Blood</b>- the Sanguine Bonds manipulate, control or trace blood both within and without<br /> <br /> <b>Cursed</b>- Sanguine Bonds are negative in nature, causing a corruptive influence on the world<br /> <br /> <b>Psychic</b>- Sanguine Bonds often mimic psychic phenomena, mostly empathic but also telekinetic<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Bashing Damage<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Vanquishment, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Finesse<br /> <br /> <b>Enemies</b>: Blood Magic [Kindred], Necromancy, Dreamwalking<br /> <br /> <u><b>Obsidian Brotherhood (S&amp;B)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: vengeance driven pyrokinetics who seeks to burn down the systematic control of the supernatural<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Pyrokinesis<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Mr Schwartz\u2019s Obsidius<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: Mr Schwartz presents himself before a victim of the supernatural, and after evaluating the candidate, if found fitting, would burn them with a scorch mark of the Obsidius representing \u201cfreedom\u201d.<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the members of the Brotherhood are imbued with the powers of fire, making them immune to all forms of fire damage.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the attempt to invoke the black fire of Pyrokinesis goes highware, setting the surrounding area on fire. If not taken care of actively, the fire would inflict the Inferno Tilt in 2 turns. Those fires can not be controlled with Pyrokinesis.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Flaming</b>- Pyrokinesis, true to its name, is able to control, generate and intensify it<br /> <br /> <b>Emotional</b>- Pyrokinesis burns with the user\u2019s emotions, becoming stronger when aligns with their aspirations, Touchstones or Anchors<br /> <br /> <b>Shaped</b>- Pyrokinesis form to the user\u2019s imagination, forming objects, structures and entities out of the flames<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Summoning, Vanquishment<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Finesse<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Theurgy [Demons], Blood Magic, Deviance<br /> <br /> <u><b>Order of the Earthly Bones (HB)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: protectors of ancient megalithic structures who keep them safe from monsters who seek to abuse them.<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Malta, France<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Gigantism<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: The Gigants<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: following an occult ceremony meant to awaken the will of the buried giants within one of the sacred sites, the hunters invest themselves with the might of the megaliths themselves<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: in order to use their connection to the giants, the members of the Order gain an Essence pull of a size equal to their Stamina. They can replenish Essence by meditating in a megalithic site (gain an amount equal to their success) or exchange a Virtue channeling from Willpower to Essence.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the giant\u2019s Essence rebels against the flesh which does not fit its might, inflicting an amount of Bashing Damage equal to their dots in the Application. (in case of a combination, use the Application with the highest value)<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Transformative</b>- Gigantism manipulates the flesh of the hunter, using it to express their supernatural power<br /> <br /> <b>Geomantic</b>- Gigantism draws power from the earth, drawing power from the flow of ley lines and sacred architecture<br /> <br /> <b>Earthmelded</b>- Gigantism mix flesh and stone together, allowing the hunter to meld with their territory<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Booning, Summoning, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Power<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Shamanism [Idigam], Dreamwalking, Sorcery<br /> <br /> <u><b>Reality Hackers (KR)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: programmers who have got access to the \u201csource god of the universe\u201d by an angel to \u201cstop instabilities in the code\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: SERAPH Algorithm<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Having their name added to the Administrator List of the SERAPH Algorithm<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the hunter must be scanned by the Algorithm, which defines their whole existence and opens their minds to the greater truth<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the Cherub Subsystem, a small device which, when connected to a computer, allows accessing different applications of the Algorithm, though only to authorized user, and allows scanning for nearby \u201canomalies\u201d through Intelligence + Computer<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: a bug in the code starts breaking up reality. A Reality Bleed Tilt is evoked until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Corresponded</b>- the SERAPH Algorithm utilises mapping between the device\u2019s commands and the entities targeted through it<br /> <br /> <b>Invasive</b>- the SERAPH Algorithm takes control over entities and aspects of reality, jamming their abilities or limiting their actions<br /> <br /> <b>Informative</b>- the SERAPH Algorithm provides and relies on information, and can\u2019t work reliably without having analysis of the target<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Divination, Summoning, Affliction<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Mental<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Alchemy [Pometheans], Theurgy, Contagion<br /> <br /> <u><b>Soldiers of the Forbidden Sun (DE:RotLI)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: mystical order dedicated for preparing to prophesied calamities by guarding ancient tombs<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: China<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Shendao<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Sleeping in the Hall of Ancestors<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: a meditation has to be performed in the Hall of Ancestors, where the participant needs to commune with the timeless world which lurks beyond the grave.<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: After breaching the boundary between life and death, the hunters are able to control their vitality, spending 1 Willpower point to hide all physical and spiritual signs of their life for a scene and becoming metaphysically \u201cdead\u201d.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the control that the hunter holds over their vitality is disturbed and starts glowing, making them visible to all supernatural entities.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Purified</b>- Shendao are based around cleansing the soul and the world around it<br /> <br /> <b>Vital</b>- Shendao bridge the boundary between life and death and are able to manipulate both<br /> <br /> <b>Internal</b>- Shendao works within the body. While it may emanate through aura, it does not construct phenomena or manipulate reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Booning, Rejuvenation<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Sorcery [Arisen], Shamanism, Necromancy<br /> <br /> <u><b>Sons of CuChulainn (DC)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: hedge lost warriors who have reached out across time to help their descendants against the darkness<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA, British Isles<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Geasa<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: accepting the traditional geis of paying tribute to the Hedge<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: entering one of the party\u2019s hedge-gates and taking their geis by cutting their hands upon the sacred spear Gae Bulg<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: under the geis the hunter gains the ability to sense the hedge gate of the party and gains the support of their time displaced warrior mentors.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the hunter\u2019s demands of fate are twisted, bestowing a curse upon them. They suffer from a bane equivalent to a spirit of Rank equal to the Endowment\u2019s Value, minimum of 1.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Verbal</b>- Geasa must be pronounced vocally and must be heard by the foe in question or a relevant witness<br /> <br /> <b>Fair</b>- Geasa only grant power equivalent to the risk which is taken by breaking it, and the more obscure the condition the more dangerous the risk becomes<br /> <br /> <b>Warborne</b>- Geasa are bestowed upon the holder, and act through them and their chosen weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Booning, Vanquishment<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Physical<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Hedge Sorcery [Huntsmen], Witchcraft, Necromancy<br /> <br /> <u><b>Valdaermen (HB)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: heirs of norse pagan tradition who believe in proving their excellence through battle against the darkness to achieve Valhalla<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Scandinavia<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Runes<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Root Rune<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: through careful use of divination, the crones of the company decipher the fate of the individual, and tattoo them with the Root Rune which describes it<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: once the Root Rune is inscribed, the hunter become masters of their own fate, bestowing -1 to all supernatural attempts to control or manipulate their minds.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the hunter\u2019s Root Rune becomes corrupted and poisons their body, bestowing upon them the moderate version of the Sick Tilt.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Inscribed</b>- Runes act upon the subject on which they are inscribed, either enhancing or enchanting it<br /> <br /> <b>Language</b>- Runes are a method of communication, and as such each Rune bestows effects appropriate to its meaning<br /> <br /> <b>Warborne</b>- Runes are the gift of Odin, the warrior god, and as such they act to fulfill success in battle<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Booning, Rejuvenation<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Physical<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Dreamwalking [Beasts], Shamanism, Necromancy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-28-2025, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T06:00:53-08:00","id":1548000,"title":"","content":"Aaaand I forgot that the site has issues with editing. Hopefully the moderators will unlock the post quickly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T17:02:37-08:00","id":1548075,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Conspiracies</b></u><br /> Conspiracies are both similar to compacts and yet fundamentally different. Like compacts, conspiracies are entities who are devouted to the Vigil, yet lack connection to any larger entity, such as a state or a religion, making them independent organizations. However, unlike compacts, conspiracies are organized and intertwined into the fabric of human society- they exist in the shadows, holding connections to governmental agencies and religious figures while still remaining apart of them. Their signs and imprints could be found everywhere if you know where to look- yet most people lack that understanding. Still, while maintaining tremendous power, conspiracies still act in the benefit of humanity- though many do have dark secrets within their cores, which they keep far from their own members, knowing that by exposing those skeletons in the closet the whole structure might fall apart. While conspiracies have a sphere of power where they are more dominant and cohesive, even outside of it they hold a lot of diffusive influence, allowing them to operate all around the world.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Aegis Kai Doru (Core)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: collectors of relics who seek to protect humanity\u2019s heritage from monsters and take vengeance against those stolen it<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Greece<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Relics<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Oath Stone<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: after being sent into a labyrinth and reaching its centre alive, the hunter has to take a sacred vow upon the Stone to fulfill their ancestral duty to fight those who have broken the world.<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the Vow directs the hunter against their ancestral enemies, giving them an Unseen Sense towards them and gain +1 for all rolls in service of the vow<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the relic malfunction, refusing to acknowledge the hunter as its master. The relic stops functioning until the end of the chapter.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Historical</b>- Relics are tied to their historical origin, manifesting a power depending on their creation and era<br /> <br /> <b>External</b>- Relics require the use of a sacred artefact, losing hold of the object removes the ability to use it<br /> <br /> <b>Objectified</b>- Relics fill a purpose fitting their design, a spear penetrates while a shield protects<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Bygone (accessible by conspiracy)<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Exorcism, Vanquishment, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Finesse<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Witchcraft [Mages], Shamanism, Sorcery<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ascending Ones (Core)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: alchemists who transform their own bodies into furnace of supernatural power in order to find the horrors of the night<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Egypt<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Elixirs<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: The Ascension Rite<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: after learning the art of alchemy, the candidate drinks a concoction of poisons, taking a leap of faith with their ability to transmute the poison into blessing. Those with appropriate faith survive, and are born again as a \u201cphoenix\u201d.<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the body of the hunter has become resistant to all toxins through alchemy, making them resilient to any mundane poison of Toxicity lower than their Stamina.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: The alchemical process is disturbed, causing an amount of bashing damage equal to the Endowment Equation Value, minimum of 1.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Alchemical</b>- Elixirs act to transmute the subject, acting through the hunter\u2019s body as a living furnace.<br /> <br /> <b>Consumed</b>- Elixirs take the form of a variety of reagents mixed with deadly poisons, which must be consumed by the hunter to activate<br /> <br /> <b>Sacred</b>- Elixirs draw their power from the themes of the Egyptian gods, allowing the hunter to harness their attributes<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Resources (replenished by conspiracy, pool corresponds to Resources merit, minimum 1)<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Booning, Rejuvenation<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Blood Magic [Vampires], Alchemy, Sorcery<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood of Ahran (VII)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: descendants of Gammorah\u2019s survivors who seek to purify the world from the terror which brought God\u2019s ire through demonic might<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Levant<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Ahranaite Sorcery<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Shaddad\u2019s Pillar<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the candidate swears an oath of loyalty to the conspiracy and allows the demon in their service to claim their heart<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the hunter\u2019s mind is clouded by Shaddad, stopping them from any supernatural or mundane attempt art betraying their conspiracy<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the demonic power of Shaddad takes over the hunter, enforcing upon them the Whispers Condition until one service is made to satisfy the demon. The more failures, the more services required<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Blood</b>- Ahranite Sorcery draws power from the hunter\u2019s blood, and it allows them to sense and manipulate that of others<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic</b>- Ahranite Sorcery emanate for Shaddad, a great fiend, and as such its outcomes are horrifying to behold<br /> <br /> <b>Vengeful</b>- Ahranite Sorcery draws upon an ancient oath of retribution, and as such it is designed to harm those who inflicted it<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Lethal Damage<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Divination, Vanquishment<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Physical<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Sorcery [Fiends], Blood Magic, Infernalism<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cainite Heresy (NS)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: zealot avengers who take radical actions to dismantle the abusing systems through which monsters thrive<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Balkans<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Rites of Denial<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Sources<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the Sources track the individual they deem as a worthy candidate due to their abuse, giving them access to the First Rites<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the hunter is found in a constant connection with the Sources, who provide them with information and ritual materials<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the protective rites fail, filling the hunter with a sense of suspicion for who might have disrupted the ritual, bestowing the Paranoid Condition upon them<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Ritualistic</b>- the Rites of Denial always demand a ritual to work- it doesn\u2019t need faith in the ritual, only its execution<br /> <br /> <b>Superstition</b>- the Rites of Denial invoke old wives tales and common superstitions, bringing them to life<br /> <br /> <b>Simple</b>- the Rites of Denial do not require complex memorisation or exotic components. A+B=C, that\u2019s it<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Blood Vial (the vial has number of thimbles equal to Status: Cainite Heresy, replenished by other members of the conspiracy)<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Affliction, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Social<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Blood Magic [Kindred], Necromancy, Sorcery<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cold Guard (D&amp;L)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: descendants of refugees of broken dreams who have abandoned all hope to keep the Darkness at bay<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Germany<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Penumbra<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: The Dreaming Ice Age<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the candidate, filled with despair and loss, travels through a dream quest which leads them to the ruins of humanity\u2019s hope bound by eternal winter, marking them with a sign of doom<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: due to the corruption of the darkness in their souls, members of the conspiracy gain +2 to all rolls meant to resist mental, spiritual or physical corruption of a supernatural source<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the Darkness manages to break through their mental boundaries, bestowing a Frostbite upon them. Once they have more Frostbites than their Resolve or Composure (the lower of the two), they are bestowed with the Fugue Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Cold</b>- Penumbra is defined by the lacking of warmth, light and voice, be it literally or metaphorically<br /> <br /> <b>Hostile</b>- Penumbra is powered by hatred and despair, using the inner darkness within the user as a power source<br /> <br /> <b>Cursed</b>- Penumbra is a dark art, taking the form of numerous curses which inflict pain and sorrow<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Booning, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Alchemy [Domemim], Slashing, Dreamwalking<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ebony Fangs (LL)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: a collection of exiles and low class individuals who hunt down the dead to stop future calamities<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA, Middle East<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Words of the Dead<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: the Laws of Irkalla define that only those who are considered \u201cdead to society\u201d or who were harmed by the dead can join the conspiracy<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the candidate, if fitting the parameters, writes their name upon an Avernian Gate, who adds them to the conspiracy\u2019s influence<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: due to allowing their names to die upon the gates of the Underworld, the hunters are protected from sympathetic magic who one which seeks to abuse their names<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the powers of death lash out upon the hunter, forcing upon them a decayed image or the scent of the grave, giving -5 to all social interactions until the end of the chapter<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Inscribed</b>- the Words of the Dead must be written upon an object, and act through the medium on which they are inscribed<br /> <br /> <b>Liminal</b>- the Words of the Dead effect either the living or the dead, and create clear distinctions between the two<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle</b>- the Words of the Dead manipulate the behaviour of the affected entities and limit their agency, but can\u2019t outright distort reality or physical phenomenon<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> F<b>avoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Exorcism, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Mental<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Necromancy [Bound], Sorcery, Blood Magic<br /> <br /> <u><b>Garde du Peuple (D&amp;L)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: egalitarian movement who constantly seeks to rally up a revolution against the rule of the supernatural<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: France<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Vox Populi<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: the Manifeste<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: going through a communal right of sharing wine and bread while taking the oath of loyalty to the conspiracy, the hunter is accepted to the Guard<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the hunter is bound by bonds of brotherhood with his companions, letting them know the general direction to the closest conspirayc member by spending a Willpower<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the fire of the revolution dies in the hunter\u2019s heart, inflicting the Demoralized Condition<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Revolution</b>- Vox Populi ia an act of rebellion against the creatures of the night, challenging their authority<br /> <br /> <b>Communal</b>- Vox Populi is a communal effort, requiring the presence and help of other hunters in teamwork<br /> <br /> <b>Liberating</b>- Vox Populi drives towards freedom, drawing from national myths and liberal values<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Summoning, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Social<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Dreamwalking [Nobles], Blood Magic, Theurgy<br /> <br /> <u><b>Keepers of Vedet (NH: N&amp;A)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: mystics who walk through dreams and souls to find monsters and defeat them within their mindscapes<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Balkans, Italy<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Caul Walking<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: being born with a caul<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: through a paganic harvest ritual, the soul of the candidate is removed from their own body, and later tethered back through a dream link. Those without a caul can\u2019t have their soul tethered by the ritual, leaving them Soulless.<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: the hunter can reach out into the Twilight, and by spending 1 Willpower they are able to see and interact with entities within the Goetic Frequency.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the attempt at astral projection goes wary, leaving the hunter suffering from dissonance between their body and soul in the form of the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Astral</b>- Caul Walking acts in the mental landscape rather than in the physical one, often requiring astral projection<br /> <br /> <b>Twilight</b>- Caul Walking acts through the Twilight, and as such its effects could be perceived in the Goetic Frequency<br /> <br /> <b>Dream</b>- Caul Walking has strong dominion over dreams and memories and is able to shape them easily<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Exorcism, Divination, Rejuvenation<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Mental<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Witchcraft [Reapers], Necromancy, Dreamwalking<br /> <br /> <u><b>Marduk Society (L:tT)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: heroic gentlemens who fight those monsters who live as false gods by harnessing humanity\u2019s hope<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Mesopotamia, US<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Sky Science<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: Marduk\u2019s Tablets- Enuma Elish<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the candidate goes through a conditioning process using the Enuma Elish machine, which subconsciously connects them to humanity\u2019s collective sense of hope<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: through their connection to the collective hope of mankind, members of the conspiracy all have Hope as a secondary Virtue, with each Virtue being able to be fulfilled once per chapter<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the hunter\u2019s faith falters seeing their failure of their own endeavours- yet their devotion to the brighter future stops them from revealing it. They suffer from the Stoic Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Hopeful</b>- Sky Science draws upon humanity\u2019s aspirations and dreams, representing what they hope to achieve<br /> <br /> <b>Sci Fi</b>- Sky Science takes the form of futuristic mechanisms, impossible inventions humans only dream about<br /> <br /> <b>Aerial</b>- Sky Science resonates with the themes of the skies themselves, such as wind and weather, both directly and metaphorically<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Divination, Vanquishment, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Social<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Dreamwalking [Leviathan], Sorcery, Theurgy<br /> <br /> <u><b>Nibiru (LL)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: ancient order of lineage of hunters chosen to bear the light open the Vigil and maintain balance between the worlds.<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: Mesopotamia<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: First Arts<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: being born to the lineage of the Nibiru<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: the hunter goes through an ancient ritual which bestows upon them the Mandate of the Vigil, allowing them to realise their heritage<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: due to their Mandate, the hunters of the conspiracy hold Honorary Status in all other organizations equal to half their Status: Nibiru rating, rounded up. This perception is instinctive, and requires direct interactions among the officials of the organization rather than allow immediate access to its resources.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the hunter\u2019s attempt to enforce their will upon the supernatural backfires, empowering the monster instead by either replenishing its supernatural resource or giving it a new Dread Power until the end of the scene<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Superstition</b>- First Arts are the original forms of magic, and often express themselves through the derivative rituals of superstitions<br /> <br /> <b>Ancient</b>- First Arts are the claimed to be the first Endowments, and deal with the basis of civilization, such as hunt and fire<br /> <br /> <b>Foci</b>- First Arts work through sympathy, and as such require some sort of a sympathetic anchor or object to work through<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Exorcism, Vanquishment, Warding<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Power<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Shamanism [Idigam], Witchcraft, Hedge Magic<br /> <br /> <u><b>Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice (P:tC)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: elitist guild of alchemists who seek to keep the art of alchemy out of unworthy hands<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: British Islands<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Aludel<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: The Rite of the Auric Chalice<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: by drinking the liquid Vitriol produced through the Rite, the soul of the hunter is transmuted from lead to gold, allowing them to grasp at the power of alchemy<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: by harvesting a monster, the hunter can refine it to produce Pyros by rolling Dexterity + Occult. Pyros could be used to heal one point of lethal damage per Pyros.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the fire rebels against the hands of the unworthy, inflicting a Wasteland on the area being equivalent to Azoth 1. In case a Wasteland is already festering, it advances it.<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Transmutative</b>- Aludel rituals allow to enforce changes upon the entity, changing its state or material<br /> <br /> <b>Objectified</b>- the Aludel contains within it the numerous alchemical reagents as well as the Pyros required, making the hunter dependent on the tool<br /> <br /> <b>Ritualistic</b>- the Aludel might contain the potential, yet the alchemical processes demand careful, mathematical procedures to function<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Pyros (pool equal to Composure or Resolve, the higher of the two, replenished through refinement)<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Booning, Summoning, Rejuvenation<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Mental<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Alchemy [Alchemists], Witchcraft, Sorcery<br /> <br /> <u><b>Survivor Lodge (TtF)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: a collection of slasher attack survivors who draw power from their own mental trauma<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Horror Within<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: survive an attempted act of murder by a slasher<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: after getting scared by the trauma, the hunter has to enter a deep meditative state where they come with terms with the desire to kill which was inflicted by their trauma<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: as part of being built to support victims of trauma, the hunter treat members of their conspiracy as Touchstones for the purpose of gaining Willpower<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the hunter is haunted by the need to kill, giving them the Obsession Condition towards murder until they slay another intelligent being<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Physical</b>- the Horror Within acts through the hunter\u2019s own physical form, and as such use it as a conduit<br /> <br /> <b>Murderous</b>- the Horror Within is the mark that a slasher left upon a victim\u2019s soul, making all abilities drawing from becoming a better killer<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane</b>- the Horror Within, while granting the semblance of supernatural power, is treated as non magical for effects which disrupt the supernatural<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Affliction, Booning, Vanquishment<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Physical<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Slashing [Slashers], Contagion, Dreamwalking<br /> <br /> <u><b>Operation Nebula (TtF)</b></u><br /> <i>Concept</i>: conspiracy theorists who try to fight the constant flux of alien invasion and stop their malicious plans<br /> <br /> <i>Sphere</i>: USA<br /> <br /> <i>Endowments</i>: Xenothechnology<br /> <br /> <i>Key</i>: The Tree of Life Scheme<br /> <br /> <i>Initiation</i>: by getting access to the darknet sites through which the conspiracy operates, they are exposed to the Tree of Life Scheme. Those who cling to rational science can not comprehend it, making it available only to those who embrace the \u201cweird\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i>: while killing a monster, an operative can roll for Intelligence + Craft in order to harvest a core from it. The core is used to produce a gizmo, and is able to be analyzed to give information about the alien in question.<br /> <br /> <i>Backlash</i>: the core can\u2019t handle the experimental pressure and is crushed, while releasing a warning sign to all nearby aliens, alerting them of the hunter\u2019s location<br /> <br /> <u>Themes</u><br /> <b>Gizmo</b>- Xenotechnology takes the form of of strange devices made through alien knowledge<br /> <br /> <b>Stolen</b>- Xenotechnology is the science of aliens, and its functions depend on the core and materials taken from them<br /> <br /> <b>Sci Fi</b>- Xenothechnology draws is themes from common science fiction tropes, fitting advance technology and psychic abilities<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: Core (each core has the Fragile Condition in relation to the hunter\u2019s Science or Occult, the highest of the two)<br /> <br /> <b>Favoured Applications</b>: Abjuration, Divination, Vanquishment<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Mental<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy</b>: Sorcery [Visitors], Eldritch Magic, Theurgy<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}